      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Commanders",
        "body": "The draft card is in, the rookies are in the building, and now comes the part every front office loves to call \"competition\" - which usually means a dozen young men fighting for three useful jobs. Washington sits 3rd in the NFC East, six games back, with a 14th seed that tells you everything about where this roster stands: respectable on paper, still too thin in the spots that matter. <strong>The most important development right now is the fresh rookie class and the immediate push to sort out who can help now, not later.</strong> That is the whole show in May. The Commanders need bodies who can play special teams, spell veterans, and survive the speed of pro football - because the 2025 receiving numbers said enough about the offense's dependence on a few names, and the draft was the chance to widen the lane. The question isn't whether the newcomers have talent; it's whether any of them can force the coaches' hand before camp hardens the depth chart. <strong>Watch the first wave of rookie practices - that's where Washington's next roster decision will be made.</strong>",
